More checks now also run on ``async for`` and ``async def``:

- ``too-many-branches`` counts ``async for`` loops.
- ``method-cache-max-size-none``, ``singledispatch-method`` and
  ``singledispatchmethod-function`` check ``async def``.
- ``bad-dunder-name`` checks ``async def`` methods. Only ``__aenter__``,
  ``__aexit__``, ``__anext__``, ``__call__`` and an async generator
  ``__aiter__`` can be ``async def``, so ``async def __enter__`` or
  ``async def __init__`` is reported.
- ``looping-through-iterator`` checks ``async for``, so an async generator
  consumed again in a nested loop is reported.
- ``useless-return``, ``inconsistent-return-statements`` and
  ``consider-using-with`` check ``async def``, and ``too-many-nested-blocks`` is
  reported for an ``async def`` even when no other function follows it.
- ``inconsistent-return-statements`` and ``useless-return`` are no longer
  skipped for a function containing a nested function with the same name.

Refs #11722
